@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=20&cursor=...` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": ...}`:
+  returns up to `limit` items ordered by `id` (default 20; allowed range 1–100).
+  Pass a non-null `next_cursor` unchanged as `cursor` to fetch the next page;
+  the final page has `next_cursor: null`. Cursors are opaque. Invalid limits or
+  cursors return HTTP 400 with an `{"error": "..."}` body.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
